features-kicker = What it does
features-title = Everything a notes app needs, nothing it doesn't.
features-notes-title = Notes & organization
features-notes-description = Star, pin and delete notes — pinned ones float to the top. Sort them into icon-tagged folders and freeform hashtags, filter by All, Starred, Pinned, folder or tag with live counts, and search titles and content instantly, locally.
features-diary-title = A diary over the same notes
features-diary-description = Every note carries its own date, independent of when it was written. Day, week and month calendars mark the days that have entries, and an optional reminder — at the time, or up to a week before — shows as a bell in both the diary and the notes list.
features-markdown-title = Markdown without preview mode
features-markdown-description = WYSIWYG editing that round-trips cleanly to Markdown. Headings, quotes, code blocks, lists, alignment, case transforms, undo and redo — plus inline links, image embeds and resizable tables with row, column and header controls.
features-sync-title = Sync you control
features-sync-description = A background engine reconciles local changes against your own Rust API over REST and Server-Sent Events: debounced batching, exponential-backoff reconnects, last-write-wins conflicts. Flip “go offline” in Settings and nothing breaks.

platforms-kicker = Every platform
platforms-title = Desktop sidebar, mobile tab bar, same notes.
platforms-description = Routing, views and components live in one shared package; each platform shell is thin. The layout adapts on its own — a persistent sidebar and top bar on desktop, a compact header with bottom tabs on mobile.
platforms-themes = Dark and light themes, with six accent colors carried through highlights, links and controls.
platforms-notes-alt = LightNotes notes list on mobile
platforms-diary-alt = LightNotes diary calendar on mobile
platforms-editor-alt = LightNotes note editor on mobile

